  "term": "monosymptomatic",
  "definition": "In this packet, monosymptomatic refers to a form of Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome that shows only a single main feature rather than the broader pattern of recurrent orofacial swelling, relapsing facial paralysis, and fissured tongue. Cheilitis granulomatosa is identified here as a monosymptomatic variant.",
